/* book exam traps: Using λ0 where λg is needed. Phase shift along a guide is 2π per λg, not per λ0, so a guide section is longer than the free-space path for the same shift. | Saying a mode 'does not exist' below cutoff. It is evanescent: the field decays as e−αz and carries no real power. | Writing a TM mode with m = 0 or n = 0. Ez ∝ sin(mπx/a)·sin(nπy/b) vanishes if either index is zero, so TM11 is the lowest TM mode. | Swapping a and b. The broad wall a sets fc10; using b is wrong by more than a factor of two for standard X-band guide. | Forgetting √εr. A filling of εr = 4 halves every fc and changes λ0 to c/(f√εr). */
