/* book exam traps: Using Q0 in QL = f0/BW when the resonator is connected. The measured bandwidth belongs to QL, not Q0. | Writing Q = BW/f0. Q is f0/BW, so wide bandwidth means low Q. | Calling a shorted λ/4 stub a series resonance. Its input impedance is infinite, so it is parallel; a shorted λ/2 line gives series resonance. | Forgetting Q0 and QL differ, and that loaded Q must be smaller than unloaded Q. | Mixing up the coupling words: Qe smaller than Q0 (g > 1) is overcoupled, not undercoupled; critical coupling is Qe = Q0, where QL = Q0/2. */
